WEBVTT

NOTE week03-clip2-causal-mask
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.205
Here are the attention scores for five
tokens: the patient denies chest pain.

2
00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:11.483
Each row is one token's query,
and each column is a key.

3
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:15.104
But a decoder is trained
to predict the next token.

4
00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:22.150
If patient could look at denies, chest,
and pain, it would simply copy the answer.

5
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.738
The causal mask fixes this.
Every score above the diagonal,

6
00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:34.150
where a query would look at a later
token, is set to minus infinity.

7
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.949
After the softmax, minus
infinity becomes zero.

8
00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:42.540
Each row now sums to one over
the tokens it is allowed to see:

9
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.750
itself and the tokens before it.

10
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:52.631
For example, the row for chest spreads
its attention over the, patient, denies,

11
00:00:52.631 --> 00:00:57.083
and chest itself, and
gives nothing to pain.

12
00:00:57.283 --> 00:01:02.853
Because of the mask, a single forward
pass trains every position at once:

13
00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:07.747
each token's output is used to
predict the token that follows it.
